# 3. API Architecture

The API follows a layered request/response architecture:

```text
Client / Frontend
       │
       ▼
API Route
       │
       ▼
Controller
       │
       ├── Request Validation
       │
       ├── Business Rules
       │
       ├── Relationship Validation
       │
       ▼
Eloquent Model
       │
       ▼
MySQL Database
       │
       ▼
API Resource
       │
       ▼
Structured JSON Response
```

The controller layer handles request processing and business logic, while API Resources control how database records are exposed to API consumers.

---

# 4. API Route Convention

The API uses a consistent resource-oriented routing convention.

### Standard CRUD structure

```text
GET     /api/{resource}/all
GET     /api/{resource}/show/{id}
POST    /api/{resource}/store
PUT     /api/{resource}/{id}
DELETE  /api/{resource}/{id}
```

Example:

```text
GET     /api/courses/all
GET     /api/courses/show/{id}
POST    /api/courses/store
PUT     /api/courses/{id}
DELETE  /api/courses/{id}
```

This convention is intentionally reused throughout the API to make endpoint discovery predictable.

