# 8. API Resources

Laravel API Resources are used to transform model data before returning it to clients.

Examples include:

```text
CourseResource
CategoryResource
InstructorResource
LessonResource
ExamResource
QuestionResource
AnswerResource
EnrollmentResource
ReviewResource
CertificateResource
ResultResource
ContactMessageResource
```

The Resource layer provides a controlled API representation instead of directly exposing Eloquent model serialization.

Conceptually:

```text
Database Model
      ↓
API Resource
      ↓
Public API Representation
```

This keeps the API contract separated from the internal database implementation.

---

# 9. Database Relationship Architecture

The API operates on a relational database structure.

The main conceptual relationships are:

```text
Users
 │
 ├── Enrollments ─────── Courses
 │
 ├── Reviews ─────────── Courses
 │
 ├── Results
 │
 └── Certificates
       
Courses
 │
 ├── Lessons
 │
 ├── Exams
 │
 └── Reviews

Exams
 │
 └── Questions
       │
       └── Answers
```

### Relationship validation

Where an endpoint receives a foreign-key identifier, the API validates that the referenced record exists before performing the database operation.

Examples:

```text
user_id   → users.id
course_id → courses.id
exam_id   → exams.id
```

This prevents invalid relational references from being accepted through the API.

