# 11. Courses API

## 11.1 Endpoints

```text
GET     /api/courses/all
GET     /api/courses/show/{id}
POST    /api/courses/store
PUT     /api/courses/{id}
DELETE  /api/courses/{id}
```

---

## 11.2 Course Data

The Course API exposes:

```text
id
title_ar
title_en
description_ar
description_en
price
image
status
duration
badge
```

Example API representation:

```json
{
    "Identity💎": 1,
    "Title_Ar🏷️": "تطوير الويب Full Stack",
    "Title_En📌": "Full Stack Web Development",
    "Description_Ar🔸": "برنامج متكامل لتعلم تطوير تطبيقات الويب...",
    "Description_En🔹": "A complete program for learning modern web development...",
    "Price🌟": "1800.00",
    "Image🖼️": "courses/example.png",
    "Status✨": "1",
    "Duration⏱️": "3 Months",
    "Badge🏷️": "Popular"
}
```

---

## 11.3 Course Creation

### Endpoint

```text
POST /api/courses/store
```

### Validation

The creation endpoint validates:

```text
id
title_ar
title_en
description_ar
description_en
price
image
status
duration
badge
```

Important rules include:

* ID must be unique.
* Titles must be strings and have a maximum length.
* Descriptions are required.
* Price must be numeric and cannot be negative.
* Image must be a valid uploaded image.
* Supported image formats include JPG, JPEG, PNG, and WEBP.
* Uploaded image size is limited to 2 MB.
* Duration is required.
* Badge is required.

### Request type

Because an image is uploaded, the request is designed for:

```text
multipart/form-data
```

---

## 11.4 Course Search

The endpoint supports dynamic searching:

```text
GET /api/courses/all?search=keyword
```

Search is performed against:

```text
title_ar
title_en
description_ar
description_en
```

### Arabic search enhancement

The implementation includes additional handling for an Arabic search variation involving the prefix:

```text
ل
```

This improves matching for common Arabic search input variations.

---

## 11.5 Course Filtering

### Popular

```text
GET /api/courses/all?filter=popular
```

Rule:

```text
badge = Popular
```

### Free

```text
GET /api/courses/all?filter=free
```

Rule:

```text
price = 0
```

### New

```text
GET /api/courses/all?filter=new
```

The latest courses are ordered by:

```text
created_at
```

and limited to three records.

---

## 11.6 Course Image Lifecycle

Course images are stored through Laravel's public filesystem disk.

### Create

```text
Upload
   ↓
Validate
   ↓
Store in courses/
   ↓
Save stored path in database
```

### Update

When a new image is uploaded:

```text
Existing Image
      ↓
Delete Old File
      ↓
Upload New File
      ↓
Save New Path
```

### Delete

When a course is deleted:

```text
Course Image
      ↓
Delete Stored File
      ↓
Delete Database Record
```

This reduces the possibility of obsolete course images remaining in storage.

