# 14. Lessons API

## 14.1 Endpoints

```text
GET     /api/lessons/all
GET     /api/lessons/show/{id}
POST    /api/lessons/store
PUT     /api/lessons/{id}
DELETE  /api/lessons/{id}
```

---

## 14.2 Lesson Data

```text
course_id
title_ar
title_en
content_ar
content_en
video_url
order
status
```

---

## 14.3 Course Relationship

Every lesson belongs to a course.

The API validates:

```text
course_id → courses.id
```

Therefore, a lesson cannot be created against a non-existing course.

---

## 14.4 Automatic Lesson Ordering

The API automatically determines the next lesson order when creating a lesson.

Conceptually:

```text
Existing maximum order
        +
        1
```

If the selected course has no lessons:

```text
order = 1
```

Example:

```text
Existing lessons:

1
2
3

New lesson:

order = 4
```

This keeps lesson sequencing consistent without requiring the client to calculate the next order manually.

---

## 14.5 Course Transfer

When updating a lesson and changing its course without explicitly providing a new order, the API calculates the next available order for the new course.

```text
Old Course
     ↓
Change Course
     ↓
Check New Course Orders
     ↓
Assign Next Order
```

---

## 14.6 Video URL Validation

The API validates the `video_url` field as a URL.

The implementation explicitly supports YouTube URLs including:

```text
youtube.com
youtu.be
```

This allows lessons to reference externally hosted educational videos.

