# 19. Reviews API

## 19.1 Endpoints

```text
GET     /api/reviews/all
GET     /api/reviews/show/{id}
POST    /api/reviews/store
PUT     /api/reviews/{id}
DELETE  /api/reviews/{id}
```

---

## 19.2 Review Data

```text
user_id
course_id
rating
comment
status
```

Example:

```json
{
    "Identity💎": 1,
    "User_Id👥": 1,
    "Course_Id🛡️": 1,
    "Rating⏳": 5,
    "Comment📋": "Excellent course with practical and useful content.",
    "Status🚀": "0"
}
```

---

## 19.3 Validation

The API validates:

```text
user_id   → existing user
course_id → existing course
rating    → numeric, minimum 1, maximum 5
comment   → required string
status    → 0 or 1
```

Therefore:

```text
rating < 1  → rejected
rating > 5  → rejected
```

---

## 19.4 Duplicate Review Prevention

A user cannot review the same course more than once.

The uniqueness condition is:

```text
user_id + course_id
```

During update, the current review is excluded from the duplicate check.

This prevents a review from accidentally conflicting with itself while still blocking duplicate reviews belonging to another record.

