# 35. CRUD Testing Strategy

Each CRUD resource follows a repeatable test lifecycle:

```text
1. GET All
      ↓
2. GET One
      ↓
3. POST Create
      ↓
4. GET Created Record
      ↓
5. PUT Update
      ↓
6. GET Updated Record
      ↓
7. DELETE
      ↓
8. GET Deleted Record
      ↓
9. Confirm 404
```

This provides a practical end-to-end verification of resource behavior.

---

# 36. Negative Testing

The API is also tested against invalid scenarios.

Examples include:

```text
Missing required field
Invalid email
Invalid numeric value
Invalid rating
Invalid foreign key
Duplicate relationship
Invalid image
Oversized image
Invalid URL
Invalid status
Non-existing ID
Business-rule violation
```

Negative testing is important because a backend should not only prove that valid requests work; it should also prove that invalid requests are rejected correctly.

