# 46. Engineering Highlights

The strongest technical aspects of the API are not limited to CRUD operations.

The implementation also demonstrates backend decision-making such as:

### Automatic sequencing

Lessons automatically receive the next available order within their course.

### Relational integrity

The API validates referenced users, courses, and exams before accepting dependent records.

### Duplicate prevention

Enrollment and review relationships are protected against duplicates.

### Domain-specific validation

Question marks are validated against the exam's total mark capacity.

### File lifecycle management

Uploaded files are deleted when replaced or when their parent resource is deleted.

### Server-controlled workflow

New contact messages automatically begin with:

```text
new
```

rather than allowing the client to arbitrarily define the initial state.

These are examples of business logic being handled by the backend rather than delegated to the frontend.

